---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TdTestCss from '../../components/head/TdTestCss.astro';
import FooterLargeCss from '../../components/head/FooterLargeCss.astro';
import TdTestScripts from '../../components/scripts/TdTestScripts.astro';
import ParallaxScripts from '../../components/scripts/ParallaxScripts.astro';
---
<Layout
    lang="en"
    path="td_test.html"
    title="TD Test – automated testing for IBM Maximo | Total Digital"
    description="TD Test is the tool for automated testing of IBM Maximo and Maximo Application Suite (MAS). Tests the interface, business logic, integrations and more."
    ogTitle="TD Test – automated testing for IBM Maximo"
    ogImage="https://www.totaldigital.se/images/og/td_test.jpg"
    ogImageAlt="TD Test home screen with test runs and results"
>
    <ParallaxScripts slot="scripts-early" lang="en" />
    <TdTestCss slot="head-css" lang="en" />
    <Fragment slot="head-after-fonts">
      <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
          "name": "TD Test",
          "url": "https://www.totaldigital.se/en/td_test.html",
          "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication",
          "description": "TD Test is the tool for automated testing of IBM Maximo and Maximo Application Suite (MAS). Tests the interface, business logic, integrations and more.",
          "inLanguage": "en-GB",
          "image": "https://www.totaldigital.se/images/og/td_test.jpg",
          "provider": {
              "@type": "Organization",
              "@id": "https://www.totaldigital.se/#organization",
              "name": "Total Digital AB",
              "url": "https://www.totaldigital.se/"
          }
      }
      </script>
    </Fragment>
    <FooterLargeCss slot="head-after-fonts" lang="en" />
    <TdTestScripts slot="scripts" lang="en" />
        <main id="content" class="showcase-top">

            <section class="introduction scrollto tdt-intro">
                <div class="row clearfix">

                    <div class="tdt-hero">
                        <div class="tdt-hero-copy">
                            <div class="section-heading has-title-icon">
                                <h1 class="section-title">TD Test</h1>
                                <p class="section-subtitle">Quality-assure your IBM Maximo</p>

                                <i class="fa-duotone fa-solid fa-clipboard-list-check title-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="tdt-hero-body">
                            <p class="tdt-lead">
                                TD Test automates testing of IBM Maximo and replaces time-consuming manual checks. A workflow is defined once and can then be tested over and over again &ndash; after upgrades, after customisations, or ahead of deployment.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tdt-intro-body">
                        <p>
                            You get a quick answer to the question that matters most: <strong>does Maximo still work the way the business expects?</strong> If something goes wrong, TD Test shows where in the flow the error occurred, what happened and what the screen looked like. The tests leave the database unchanged, so they can be repeated without affecting your data.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            TD Test supports both IBM Maximo 7.x and IBM Maximo Application Suite (MAS), and the same tests can be run against either version. That makes it easy to verify that processes and customisations still work after an upgrade.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Unlike traditional testing tools, TD Test works directly against Maximo without going through the browser. That gives faster, more stable tests that do not need rewriting when the interface changes.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <a href="#capabilities" class="scroll-cue" data-scroll-to
                        aria-label="Read more about Capabilities"><span class="scroll-cue-label">Read more</span><i class="fa-solid fa-chevrons-down" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>

                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="capabilities" class="primary-color scrollto clearfix">
                <div class="row clearfix">

                    <div class="section-heading">
                        <h2 class="section-kicker">CAPABILITIES</h2>
                        <p class="section-title">What can TD Test do?</p>
                        <p class="section-subtitle">"Testing Maximo with the help of Maximo." <br>TD Test works from within Maximo, allowing it to test the interface, business logic, integrations and more.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tdt-trio">
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="card-title">Test what matters</h3>
                            <p>TD Test can automate tests of:</p>
                            <ul class="tdt-list">
                                <li>Maximo's user interface and business logic</li>
                                <li>Integrations with other systems</li>
                                <li>Your own customisations and functions</li>
                                <li>Complete business processes</li>
                                <li>Work flows containing several users, for example approval and handover</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <h3 class="card-title">See exactly what went wrong</h3>
                            <p>After every run TD Test gives you:</p>
                            <ul class="tdt-list">
                                <li>A result for each test step</li>
                                <li>Error messages and relevant logs</li>
                                <li>Screenshots from every step</li>
                                <li>History of earlier test runs</li>
                                <li>Automatic reporting to e.g. Teams</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <h3 class="card-title">Run it on your terms</h3>
                            <p>TD Test gives you the flexibility to:</p>
                            <ul class="tdt-list">
                                <li>Run single tests or whole test groups</li>
                                <li>Schedule recurring runs</li>
                                <li>Start tests directly from the browser</li>
                                <li>Integrate with e.g. Jenkins</li>
                                <li>Control the log level per test without affecting Maximo's normal settings</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-1 tdt-tour">
                        <div class="image-carousel" data-image-carousel>
                            <div class="image-carousel-track">

                                <figure class="image-carousel-slide">
                                    <img class="tdt-shot" src="../images/product-images/td-test/landing-page.webp"
                                        width="1920" height="1416" loading="lazy"
                                        alt="The TD Test start page, with test suites and recent runs" data-zoomable>
                                    <figcaption><strong>The start page</strong> &ndash; an overview of where things stand right now.
                                    </figcaption>
                                </figure>

                                <figure class="image-carousel-slide">
                                    <img class="tdt-shot" src="../images/product-images/td-test/test-runs-history.webp" width="1920"
                                        height="1416" loading="lazy" alt="History of earlier test runs in TD Test"
                                        data-zoomable>
                                    <figcaption><strong>Run history</strong> &ndash; earlier runs, so you can follow quality over time.</figcaption>
                                </figure>

                                <figure class="image-carousel-slide">
                                    <img class="tdt-shot" src="../images/product-images/td-test/test-run-report.webp"
                                        width="1920" height="1416" loading="lazy"
                                        alt="Details of a test run in TD Test" data-zoomable>
                                    <figcaption><strong>Run details</strong> &ndash; the result for every test that was part of the run.</figcaption>
                                </figure>

                                <figure class="image-carousel-slide">
                                    <img class="tdt-shot" src="../images/product-images/td-test/test-case-report.webp"
                                        width="1920" height="1416" loading="lazy"
                                        alt="Details of a single test case in TD Test, with source code" data-zoomable>
                                    <figcaption><strong>Test case details</strong> &ndash; step by step, with the test's source code alongside so you can see
                                    what was tested.</figcaption>
                                </figure>

                                <figure class="image-carousel-slide">
                                    <img class="tdt-shot" src="../images/product-images/td-test/maximo-gui.webp"
                                        width="1920" height="1416" loading="lazy"
                                        alt="Saved screenshot of Maximo from a test step" data-zoomable>
                                    <figcaption><strong>Saved Maximo view</strong> &ndash; exactly what Maximo's interface showed at that test step.</figcaption>
                                </figure>

                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="features" class="scrollto clearfix">
                <div class="row clearfix">

                    <div class="section-heading">
                        <h2 class="section-kicker">BENEFITS</h2>
                        <p class="section-title">Why TD Test?</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-1 area-band">

                        <div class="area-band-item">
                            <div class="tdt-icon"><i class="fa-duotone fa-solid fa-gauge-high" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                            <h3>Fast</h3>
                            <p>TD Test works directly against Maximo, without the detour through a browser. That gives tests that can run up to 100 times faster.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="area-band-item">
                            <div class="tdt-icon"><i class="fa-duotone fa-solid fa-shield-check" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                            <h3>Stable</h3>
                            <p>TD Test is not affected by changes to Maximo's interface or by browser behaviour. The tests are more stable and need less maintenance as Maximo changes.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="area-band-item">
                            <div class="tdt-icon"><i class="fa-duotone fa-solid fa-piggy-bank" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                            <h3>Cost-effective</h3>
                            <p>TD Test needs no dedicated hardware and can run as a container in an environment you already have. Fast implementation and less test maintenance deliver benefit quickly.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="area-band-item">
                            <div class="tdt-icon"><i class="fa-duotone fa-solid fa-list-check" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                            <h3>Easy to use</h3>
                            <p>TD Test follows the same logic and the same names as Maximo, which makes the tests easy to create and to follow. Clear reporting shows exactly where the error occurs.</p>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="primary-color scrollto clearfix">
                <div class="row clearfix">

                    <div class="section-heading">
                        <h2 class="section-kicker">COMPARISON</h2>
                        <p id="comparison-heading" class="section-title">TD Test vs. browser-based testing</p>
                    </div>

